//! fail
// The tail of D4.5: i32 if it fits, otherwise i64, otherwise an error. The
// error half, for an untyped expression that folded to no value and for one
// that folded. run/constants/012_untyped_constant_wider_than_i32.ft holds the
// i64 half beside it.
//
// A shift whose count is a variable carries its constant to the default type
// (type-system.md 10.5), so the first two lines are reported against i64 and
// name the constant. Both were accepted in silence until 2026-09-13: the
// constant has no default type, and the shift dropped the whole expression
// before any context could read it.
//
// The last two lines never reach a type: `-9223372036854775809` leaves the
// range untyped folding works in, `[-2^63, 2^64 - 1]` (D4.4), and
// `9223372036854775808` is inside that range and outside i64. The last of the
// four drew a second diagnostic until 2026-09-14, "the expression expects
// <error>, not a constant". The type is poisoned by the first, and D14.2 silences every later
// diagnostic on a poisoned type, so the context now says nothing. The harness
// judges a line and not a count, so it cannot see that removal; the count
// stands in test/check_poison_test.c and in test/fort/check_test.ft.
fn z(i32 v) i32 {
    return v;
}

fn main() i32 {
    i32 n = z(0);
    println(9223372036854775808 << n); //! error: constant 9223372036854775808 does not fit i64
    println(18446744073709551615 << n); //! error: constant 18446744073709551615 does not fit i64
    println(-9223372036854775809 << n); //! error: constant expression out of range
    println(9223372036854775808); //! error: constant expression out of range
    // The other half of the guard that lets the four lines above be reported:
    // a poisoned operand that is no untyped constant still stops at the shift.
    // This line holds the diagnostic and not the count. A shift that let the
    // error type through adds "'<<' takes an integer left operand" on this same
    // line, and the harness judges a line and not a count, so this file stays
    // green under that mutation. The count is asserted where a test can read it,
    // in check_const_test.c and in test/fort/check_test.ft.
    println(nosuch << n); //! error: unknown name 'nosuch'
    return 0;
}
